        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "The scatterplot above shows the federal-mandated minimum wage every 10 years between 1940 and 2010. A line of best fit is shown, and its equation is *y* =0.096*x* - 0.488. What does the line of best fit predict about the increase in the minimum wage over the 70-year period?"
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "kind": "gengdu-export",
        "sourceSetId": "gengdu-offline-52970e7f57bb4e4f977db0eff7b608e2",
        "sourceQuestionId": "8900451",
        "url": "https://gengdu.shanmaostar.com"
      },
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "choice-a",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "Each year between 1940 and 2010, the average increase in minimum wage was 0.096 dollars."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-b",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "Each year between 1940 and 2010, the average increase in minimum wage was 0.49 dollars."
